"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H0495","lemma":"אֶלָּסָר","tr":"el·la·sar","gloss":"Ellasar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H0569","lemma":"אַמְרָפֶל","tr":"am·ra·phel","gloss":"Amraphel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H5880","lemma":"עֵין מִשְׁפָּט","tr":"en mish·pat","gloss":"En-mishpat","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H6255","lemma":"עַשְׁתְּרֹת קַרְנַיִם","tr":"ash·te·rot qar·na·yim","gloss":"Ashteroth-karnaim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"His kingdom began in Babylon, Erech, Accad, and Calneh, in the land of Shinar.","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"And Lot looked out and saw that the whole plain of the Jordan, all the way to Zoar, was well watered like the garden of the Lord, like the land of Egypt. (This was before the Lorddestroyed Sodom and Gomorrah.)","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":2,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"just as He had done for the descendants of Esau who lived in Seir, when He destroyed the Horites from before them. They drove them out and have lived in their place to this day.","from":6},{"book":"DEU","chapter":29,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"All its soil will be a burning waste of sulfur and salt, unsown and unproductive, with no plant growing on it, just like the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah, Admah and Zeboiim, which the LORD overthrew in His fierce anger.","from":2},{"book":"2CH","chapter":20,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then some men came and told Jehoshaphat, “A vast army is coming against you from Edom, from beyond the Sea; they are already in Hazazon-tamar” (that is, En-gedi).","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and the borders of Canaan extended from Sidon toward Gerar as far as Gaza, and then toward Sodom, Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboiim, as far as Lasha.","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And while he was dwelling in the Wilderness of Paran, his mother got a wife for him from the land of Egypt.","from":6},{"book":"NUM","chapter":34,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the border will go down along the Jordan and end at the Salt Sea. This will be your land, defined by its borders on all sides.”","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"13-16":{"people":[{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"amorites-h0567","name":"Amorites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"aner-h6063g","name":"Aner","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mamre","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"eshcol-h0812g","name":"Eshcol","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mamre","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"father-of-mamre-h4471i","name":"father of Mamre","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"hebrews-h5680","name":"Hebrews","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"mamre-h4471h","name":"Mamre","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Eshcol","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"lot-h3876g","name":"Lot","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Haran","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"places":[{"id":"dan-h1835g","name":"Dan","kind":"place","brief":"In Dan","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"damascus-h1834","name":"Damascus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"hobah-h2327","name":"Hobah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15}],"words":[{"base":"H0087","lemma":"אַבְרָם","tr":"av·ram","gloss":"Abram","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":61},{"base":"H0251","lemma":"אָח","tr":"ach","gloss":"brother: male-sibling","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":629},{"base":"H7399","lemma":"רְכוּשׁ","tr":"re·khush","gloss":"property","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":28},{"base":"H7291","lemma":"רָדַף","tr":"ra·daph","gloss":"to pursue","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":143},{"base":"H6063","lemma":"עָנֵר","tr":"a·ner","gloss":"Aner","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H0812","lemma":"אֶשְׁכֹּל","tr":"esh·kol","gloss":"Eshcol","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H0436","lemma":"אֵלוֹן","tr":"e·lon","gloss":"(Diviners') Oak","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H1571","lemma":"גַּם","tr":"gam","gloss":"also","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":769},{"base":"H4471","lemma":"מַמְרֵא","tr":"mam·re","gloss":"Mamre","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H3211","lemma":"יָלִיד","tr":"ya·lid","gloss":"born","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"So Abram moved his tent and went to live near the Oaks of Mamre at Hebron, where he built an altar to the Lord.","from":13},{"book":"JDG","chapter":18,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"They named it Dan, after their forefather Dan, who was born to Israel—though the city was formerly named Laish.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Abram continued, “Behold, You have given me no offspring, so a servant in my household will be my heir.”","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the Jebusites, the Amorites, the Girgashites,","from":13},{"book":"GEN","chapter":11,"verse":27,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"This is the account of Terah. Terah became the father of Abram, Nahor, and Haran. And Haran became the father of Lot. During his father Terahʼs lifetime, Haran died in his native land, in Ur of the Chaldeans. And Abram and Nahor took wives for themselves. Abramʼs wife was named Sarai, and Nahorʼs wife was named Milcah; she was the daughter of Haran, who was the father of both Milcah and Iscah. But Sarai was barren; she had no children. And Terah took his son Abram, his grandson Lot son of Haran, and his daughter-in-law Sarai the wife of Abram, and they set out from Ur of the Chaldeans for the land of Canaan. But when they arrived in Haran, they settled there.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"I will make you into a great nation, and I will bless you; I will make your name great, so that you will be a blessing.","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Abram took his wife Sarai, his nephew Lot, and all the possessions and people they had acquired in Haran, and set out for the land of Canaan. When they came to the land of Canaan,","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"He treated Abram well on her account, and Abram acquired sheep and cattle, male and female donkeys, menservants and maidservants, and camels.","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"17-20":{"people":[{"id":"chedorlaomer-h3540","name":"Chedorlaomer","kind":"person","brief":"Mesopotamian king","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"melchizedek-h4442","name":"Melchizedek","kind":"person","brief":"A priest/king","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":19}],"places":[{"id":"king-s-valley-h4428l","name":"King's Valley","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"shaveh-h7740","name":"Shaveh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"sodom-h5467","name":"Sodom","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"words":[{"base":"H5945","lemma":"עֶלְיוֹן","tr":"el·yon","gloss":"high","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":53},{"base":"H4442","lemma":"מַלְכִּי־צֶ֫דֶק","tr":"mal·ki-tse·deq","gloss":"Melchizedek","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H0410","lemma":"אֵל","tr":"el","gloss":"God","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":241},{"base":"H1288","lemma":"בָּרַךְ","tr":"ba·rakh","gloss":"to bless","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":330},{"base":"H6010","lemma":"עֵ֫מֶק","tr":"e·meq","gloss":"Valley (of Achor)","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":69},{"base":"H7740","lemma":"שָׁוֵה","tr":"sha·veh","gloss":"Shaveh","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H8004","lemma":"שָׁלֵם","tr":"sha·lem","gloss":"Salem","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H4042","lemma":"מָגַן","tr":"ma·gan","gloss":"to deliver","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H3540","lemma":"כְּדׇרְלָעֹמֶר","tr":"ke·dor·la·o·mer","gloss":"Chedorlaomer","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H3318","lemma":"יָצָא","tr":"ya·tsa","gloss":"to come out: come","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1067}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"HEB","chapter":6,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"where Jesus our forerunner has entered on our behalf. He has become a high priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.","from":18},{"book":"HEB","chapter":7,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"Without father or mother or genealogy, without beginning of days or end of life, like the Son of God, he remains a priest for all time.","from":18},{"book":"PSA","chapter":110,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"The LORD has sworn and will not change His mind: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”","from":18},{"book":"HEB","chapter":5,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"And in another passage God says: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”","from":18},{"book":"HEB","chapter":7,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"But Melchizedek, who did not trace his descent from Levi, collected a tenth from Abraham and blessed him who had the promises.","from":19},{"book":"HEB","chapter":7,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"And indisputably, the lesser is blessed by the greater.","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"But Abram replied to the king of Sodom, “I have raised my hand to the LordGod Most High, Creator of heaven and earth,","from":19},{"book":"HEB","chapter":5,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"and was designated by God as high priest in the order of Melchizedek.","from":18}],"notes":[{"id":"gen-14-melchizedek","title":"Melchizedek, priest of God Most High","kind":"type"}],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"21-24":{"people":[{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":3,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"aner-h6063g","name":"Aner","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mamre","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"eshcol-h0812g","name":"Eshcol","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mamre","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"places":[{"id":"sodom-h5467","name":"Sodom","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"mamre-h4471g","name":"Mamre","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"words":[{"base":"H0087","lemma":"אַבְרָם","tr":"av·ram","gloss":"Abram","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":61},{"base":"H5467","lemma":"סְדֹם","tr":"se·dom","gloss":"Sodom","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":39},{"base":"H2506","lemma":"חֵ֫לֶק","tr":"che·leq","gloss":"portion","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":67},{"base":"H3947","lemma":"לָקַח","tr":"la·qach","gloss":"to take: take","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":966},{"base":"H9032","lemma":"ךְ","tr":"kh","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":333},{"base":"H8288","lemma":"שְׂרוֹךְ","tr":"se·rokh","gloss":"thong","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6063","lemma":"עָנֵר","tr":"a·ner","gloss":"Aner","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H0812","lemma":"אֶשְׁכֹּל","tr":"esh·kol","gloss":"Eshcol","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H2339","lemma":"חוּט","tr":"chut","gloss":"thread","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H4471","lemma":"מַמְרֵא","tr":"mam·re","gloss":"Mamre","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":5,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But Elisha replied, “As surely as the LORD lives, before whom I stand, I will not accept it.” And although Naaman urged him to accept it, he refused.","from":23},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then an escapee came and reported this to Abram the Hebrew. Now Abram was living near the Oaks of Mamre the Amorite, a brother of Eshcol and Aner, all of whom were bound by treaty to Abram.","from":24},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and he blessed Abram and said: “Blessed be Abram by God Most High, Creator of heaven and earth,","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and blessed be God Most High, who has delivered your enemies into your hand.” Then Abram gave Melchizedek a tenth of everything.","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Abram was ninety-nine years old, the Lordappeared to him and said, “I am God Almighty. Walk before Me and be blameless.","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":23,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now, therefore, swear to me here before God that you will not deal falsely with me or my children or descendants. Show to me and to the country in which you reside the same kindness that I have shown to you.” And Abraham replied, “I swear it.” But when Abraham complained to Abimelech about a well that Abimelechʼs servants had seized, Abimelech replied, “I do not know who has done this. You did not tell me, so I have not heard about it until today.” So Abraham brought sheep and cattle and gave them to Abimelech, and the two men made a covenant.","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Abraham planted a tamarisk tree in Beersheba, and there he called upon the name of the Lord, the Eternal God.","from":22},{"book":"EXO","chapter":6,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And I will bring you into the land that I swore to give to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. I will give it to you as a possession. I am the LORD!’”","from":22}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}